In the following we describe our approach to incorporate real agents behaviors and interactions in CARLA autonomous driving simulator [7] by using immersive virtual reality and human motion capture systems. The idea, schematically represented in Fig. 1, is to integrate a subject in the simulated scenarios using CARLA and Unreal Engine 4 (UE4), with real time feedback of the pose of his head and body, and including positional sound, attempting to create a virtual experience that is so realistic that the participant feels as though they are physically present in that world and subconsciously accepts it as such (i.e., maximize

